# Cross-origin isolation for the web editor only: SharedArrayBuffer (wasm
# pthreads) requires COOP+COEP, and scoping it here keeps third-party embeds
# working everywhere else on the site. require-corp rather than credentialless:
# Safari implements only require-corp, and the editor can satisfy it — its
# direct subresources are same-origin, engine fetches run in CORS mode, and
# the in-app Web panel's iframe carries its own `credentialless` attribute
# (page-level COEP never governed nested documents). Safari loses only the
# cross-origin Web panel (no iframe credentialless there) but gains the
# editor itself.
# Both spellings: the assets host 307-redirects webeditor.html to the
# extensionless pretty URL, and headers match the path actually served.
#
# HTML is never stored: a visit after a deploy must read the stamped asset
# revision. Assets revalidate so a stale HTML that still names the unversioned
# files cannot keep a previous wasm forever.
/webeditor
  Cache-Control: no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp

/webeditor.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp

/webeditor-assets/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
